cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Atlas: a census of communal living"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Heart of Ecovillages"
version: "2026-07-30"
date-released: "2026-07-30"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
url: "https://heartofecovillages.org/#atlas"
abstract: >-
  A global dataset of 6,246 intentional communities across 137 countries,
  compiled and deduplicated from roughly forty published directories in nine
  languages, and individually verified against public web evidence. Includes
  ecovillages, cohousing, monastic and other communal traditions, kibbutzim,
  care communities, anarchist and autonomous projects, co-living labs and
  Transition Towns, alongside communities affiliated with no network. Each
  entry carries a verification stamp and a coordinate provenance. Coordinates
  are deliberately fuzzed to roughly 1.1 km to protect residential privacy.
keywords:
  - intentional communities
  - ecovillages
  - cohousing
  - communal living
  - housing cooperatives
  - social movements
